      "Type 317 is chromium-nickel austenitic stainless steel having phenomenal corrosion resistance. A high content of molybdenum in this grade improves its pitting resistance property. This grade has high tensile, as well as a creep strength feature. Type 317 is more robust than 304 stainless steel. You can hot work this alloy between 2100-2300F. This alloy is not suitable for heat treatment but can be cold worked, which increases its strength as well as hardness.",
