      "SS 304L is the low carbon version of 304 and can be used at the as-welded condition, even at the tough corrosive conditions. 304L is having very good welding properties and is welded by all standard techniques. In order to relieve stress at the time of severe forming/spinning, welding might be followed through annealing.",
      "SS 304H is the alloy containing carbon in greater proportion. This steel is right for the applications wherein the greater temperature is available. This ally is having very good yielding and tensile strength.",
