      "Strength to weight ratio is best in titanium Grade 2 of any corrosion-resistant material. One of the most common Titanium is Grade 2 and it is used for offshore oil installation water pipelines, bleaching plants in the paper industry and condenser tubing, and also used as heat exchangers for some applications. Titanium Grade2 has good density and also a good conductor of thermal conductivity. And the modulus of elasticity is also excellent and the melting point is 3040 Degree Celsius in this grade. It has an ultimate tensile and yield strength. It is available in hot rolled, dull finish, smooth finish, bright cold rolled matte finish and various finishes available.",
      "Titanium Gr 2 Forged Fittings can be used in any application in which corrosion resistance and formability are necessary and the requirement of strength is average. To achieve moderate raise in strength it is heat treatable. Titanium Gr 2 Forged Fittings typically include applications in petroleum refining, biomedical, heat exchangers, and also include chemical processes. It is commonly found in the annealed condition.",
      "The material is duly tested to make them according to the temperature of the outside world. The test includes Chemical Analysis, Flattening test. Micro and macro test, positive material identification, hardness test .flaring test, etc. Packing is done according to avoid the last stages of damage and also according to the customer need. Pallet packaging and plywood cases packing are mostly preferred.",
